# Point the React demo at a real media API instead of the in-memory seed.
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored by Vite) and restart the dev server.
#
# The base URL must include the `/api/` prefix and may end with a slash:
#   VITE_MEDIA_API=http://pdf-api.test/api/
#
# The backend needs to expose, relative to that base:
#   GET    medias                  ?page&rowsPerPage&filters={...}
#   POST   medias                  multipart, field `file[]` + optional folder_id
#   PUT    medias/:id              { filename?, alt?, tags?, folder_id? }
#   DELETE medias/:id
#   GET    media-folders           ?rowsPerPage=0  (0 = all)
#   POST   media-folders           { name }
#   PUT    media-folders/:id       { name }
#   DELETE media-folders/:id
#
# …and must send CORS headers for the dev-server origin. Leave unset to run
# offline against the seeded in-memory adapter.
VITE_MEDIA_API=
